# xrandr --output HEADLESS-2 --right-of HEADLESS-1, captured 2026-09-10 THROUGH the proxy on a TWO-HEAD headless sway
# (`WLR_HEADLESS_OUTPUTS=2`, HEADLESS-2 at x=1280 and HEADLESS-1 at x=2560):
# sway -> Xwayland 24.1.10 -> `python3 -m xw11 --foreground` -> the recorder
# scratchpad/b7/rec.py -> xrandr 1.5.3. RANDR major 139, root 0x236, crtcs 0x20
# (output 0x21, HEADLESS-2) and 0x22 (output 0x23, HEADLESS-1), mode 0x43 =
# 1280x720 and 0x44 = 800x600.
#
# **This is R2.** Design section 7.7 INFERRED the multi-output shape from
# xrandr's `apply()` and said batch 7 must measure it before the coalescing
# rule was trusted for more than one crtc. It is measured, and the inference
# was right: one disable for the crtc that moves, ONE SetScreenSize, then one
# enable per crtc -- all inside the one grab, and the whole layout
# normalised to min x = 0 by xrandr itself before it is sent.
#
# Exit status 0, and sway afterwards: HEADLESS-1 at 0, HEADLESS-2 at 1280, both 1280x720.
# 31 requests, one per line.
